{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheoryArchimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DilogTheoryArchimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Reflection"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.SuslinDilogTheory.reflection_of_continuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.SuslinDilogTheory.reflection_of_continuous","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DilogTheoryArchimedean.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**Reflection for every continuous archimedean instance.** Off `{0,1}` it follows from\nrigidity: such an instance is `c · D`, and `D` is reflection-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.blochWigner_anharmonic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.blochWigner_anharmonic","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DilogTheoryArchimedean.lean#L51-L57","doc":"**The anharmonic orbit of Bloch–Wigner, unconditionally.** Reflection oddness is\n`FiveTermProof.blochD_one_sub`; the rest is the algebra of `SuslinDilogTheory.anharmonic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.SuslinDilogTheory.eq_mul_blochWigner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.SuslinDilogTheory.eq_mul_blochWigner","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DilogTheoryArchimedean.lean#L41-L48","doc":"**Rigidity of the archimedean instances.** A `SuslinDilogTheory ℂ ℝ` that is continuous\noff `{0,1}` and odd under conjugation is a real multiple of Bloch–Wigner. This is PR #7946's\n`BlochSuslinRigidity` instance, read as a statement about the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.blochWigner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.blochWigner","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DilogTheoryArchimedean.lean#L33-L38","doc":"**The Bloch–Wigner instance.** The analysis is `blochD_inv` and the five-term relation\n`blochWignerFiveTerm_blochD` (PR #7946). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.rogers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DilogTheory.rogers","kind":"def","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DilogTheoryArchimedean.lean#L19-L25","doc":"**The real instance.** Rogers' `L` on `(0,1)`. The analysis is exactly\n`rogersL_reflection` (Euler reflection) and `rogersL_fiveTerm` (Abel). ","signatureChunk":0}]}